Tests: a fixture with one skipped path per reason (`ignored`, `binary`, `size_cap`, `unsupported_ext`, `unreadable`), a `src-old/` sibling that a `src` prefix must not match, two languages with test nodes, and three unresolved rows with different `evidence_kind` values.

Port `src/shared/domain/resolve.ts` (479 lines) and `neighbors.ts` (259 lines). Signatures:
```rust
pub const CANDIDATE_CAP: usize = 5;
pub const RESOLUTION_STEPS: [&str; 5] = ["exact_qn", "exact_name", "dotted_tail", "path", "decorator"];
pub struct ResolveOptions { pub kinds: Option<Vec<String>>, pub path: Option<String> }
pub enum Resolution { Ok { step: ResolutionStep, node: NodeRow },
  Ambiguous { step: ResolutionStep, candidates: Vec<ResolutionCandidate>, candidates_total: usize, candidates_shown: usize },
  NotFound { near_misses: Vec<ResolutionCandidate> } }
pub fn resolve(src: &dyn ResolutionSource, query: &str, opts: &ResolveOptions) -> Resolution;
pub fn resolution_source(conn: &Conn) -> impl ResolutionSource;
pub const EXPAND_DEPTH_MAX: u8 = 4;
pub fn clamp_depth(depth: i64) -> u8;                   // 1..=4
pub fn expand(src: &dyn NeighbourSource, node_id: i64, direction: Direction, depth: u8, kinds: Option<&[String]>) -> GroupedNeighbors;
```
Rules that must not drift: the five steps are tried in order with their scores; the `path` filter (`is_under_prefix`) applies INSIDE every step and to near misses, before the cap; `candidates_total` is the pre-cap tie count and `candidates_shown` the returned length, and every `why` string is built from `candidates_total`; an ambiguous set must actually tie. `expand` returns groups `{kind, tier, items}` ordered as the TypeScript side orders them, deduplicating by `(kind, qn)` while keeping the closest hop, and reports `depth` clamped to 1..=4.
Tests: every case of `tests/domain.test.ts` for resolution (all five steps, ambiguity above the cap, path filter, near misses), plus expansion at depth 1 and 3, both directions, with a dedup case.

