`assemble` must: derive `complete` from `failed == 0 && skipped == 0` (copy the TypeScript predicate exactly), return `not_indexed` trimmed to the scope's prefixes, carry `tests` only when the caller asked for it, and return the same `unresolved` rows it counted so `coverage.unresolved_edges == unresolved.len()` cannot disagree.
`score` must: weigh the same changed/impacted facts with the same weights and thresholds, emit `drivers` in the same order and wording, and — the filed bug — emit NO test-coverage driver and no `test_gaps_total: 0` claim when the change set is empty. A clean tree reports `{score: 0, band: "low", drivers: []}`.
