```
Copy exactly: the git invocation `git --no-pager --no-optional-locks -c credential.helper= -c core.askpass= -C <root> <args>`, the 30 s timeout with SIGKILL, and the rename-aware `diff --name-status -z` parse that `diff.ts` now uses (`R`/`C` records produce ONE entry carrying `from`; `diff.ts` no longer passes `--no-renames`). Note the one deliberate difference: `src/indexer/worker.ts:750-755` still passes `--no-renames` for its own changed-file list — that call is TASK-046's and keeps its flag, so do not 'harmonise' the two.
A single unparseable record is skipped and recorded in `unmatched` (never nulls the whole parse), an untracked file is an entry with `state: untracked`, and a git failure sets `degraded` rather than throwing.
